// P1.10: structured Headers in std/net/http.dva — a growable array of
// "Name: Value" lines with append / case-insensitive lookup / render,
// replacing the flat "K: V\r\n" string for programs that need to read a
// header back.

#use net/http
#use io

// The round-trip builds a set, reads one value back case-insensitively, and
// renders the wire form.
io::out $ http::headers_roundtrip("hi")

// A longer body: Content-Length tracks the body's byte length.
io::out $ http::headers_roundtrip("hello world")
